Restricted result; no published source was checked; novelty not verified. The odd perfect
number conjecture remains open.

For each prime receiver `u` with `271 ≤ u ≤ 347`, a certificate `(A, L)` accepted by
`ReceiverSieve.packRow` (kernel evaluation): the absent primes `A` with their divisor lists, and
the envelope `L`. The three parts are checked in the kernel through the fast tests of
`OddPerfect.EulerIndexPairReceiverFastEnv` and their implication theorems. The set of kept pure
row lengths is computed by the checker from `u`. Each receiver needs its own finite certificate;
no uniform statement over all receivers is proved.
-/

